Or contribute to the BF, where this will presumably come up. I would
have sent this to the BF forum, but I'm not sure who you are, so can't
be sure you're there.

Re blotation, removing little-used role places is not a politically 
acceptable solution. Usage has proved that creating lujvo is not a
workable solution either; people just ignore unwanted places.

Re tolylogji, it is a basic principle of Lojban design that concision
is inversely proportional to precision, and ellipsis and vagueness
generally go hand in hand. The vagueness in question -- between
alternative tavla predicates -- is resolvable by avoiding the 
ellipsis.

